      "Most \"Instagram Ads vs Google Ads\" comparisons are written generically, but the right answer genuinely depends on the kind of business asking. A restaurant or retail shop in Chennai has different buying behavior than a B2B service or a clinic — food and fashion are visual, impulse-friendly, and discovery-driven in a way that most services aren't. Here's the comparison specifically for that kind of business.",
      "### How Customers Actually Discover a Restaurant or Retail Shop",
      "A lot of restaurant and retail discovery isn't \"I searched for it\" — it's \"I saw it and now I want it.\" Someone scrolling Instagram sees a plate of biryani or a new outfit and decides they want it right now, with no prior search intent. That's fundamentally different from someone actively typing \"biryani near me\" into Google because they've already decided they're hungry and are choosing between known options. Both behaviors are real and common — which is why the right answer is rarely \"pick one,\" but it's worth understanding which one dominates for your specific business.",
      "### What Instagram Ads Are Genuinely Good At",
      "Instagram (and Meta Ads generally) is built for visual discovery and impulse decisions — showing your food, your storefront, your new stock to people who weren't actively looking but get genuinely tempted by a good photo or short video. It's strong for building brand recognition, showcasing new menu items or collections, and reaching people based on interests and location even before they've formed intent to buy. For a visually appealing restaurant or retail shop, this is often the stronger top-of-funnel channel.",
      "### What Google Ads Are Genuinely Good At",
      "Google Ads captures people who've already formed intent — searching \"best north indian restaurant tambaram\" or \"formal shirts shop near me\" means someone has already decided what they want and is choosing where to get it. That's a warmer, more ready-to-convert search than a scroll-stopping Instagram ad, but you're only reaching people who are already actively searching, not the much larger pool who'd want your product if they simply saw it.",
