      "For most restaurants and retail shops in Chennai starting out, a reasonable approach is Instagram Ads for visual discovery and brand-building (new dishes, offers, behind-the-scenes content) paired with a well-optimized, free Google Business Profile to capture the \"already decided, searching now\" traffic — reserving paid Google Ads budget for once you've confirmed there's real, high-intent local search volume worth paying for. Test small on both before committing a large budget to either.",
      "### What Actually Matters More Than the Platform Choice",
      "Whichever platform you use, the offer and the follow-through matter more than the platform itself. A vague ad (\"visit us today!\") underperforms a specific one (a named dish, a real discount, a clear address and hours) on either platform. And an ad that drives people to a slow website or an unanswered WhatsApp message wastes the ad spend regardless of which platform sent them there.",
      "- Is your business more visual and impulse-driven (food, fashion, decor) or more search-driven (someone already knows what they want)?\n- Is your Google Business Profile fully optimized before you consider paying for Google Ads?\n- Are your ads showing a specific, real offer rather than a generic \"visit us\" message?\n- Does your ad lead to a fast website or a monitored WhatsApp number, not a dead end?\n- Have you tested a small budget on both platforms before committing heavily to one?",
